        "id": "node-1792685829334",
        "instruction": {
          "text": "John Doe is verified. Their account with Alpha Bank has a balance of {{balance_formatted}} as of {{balance_as_of}}. Say the date naturally, like \"as of October 22\"; never read out the timestamp.\n\nAny terms within these limits are acceptable:\n- The total paid is at least 80% of {{balance}} dollars. Work out that minimum first, and never offer or accept a lower total, even if asked.\n- It's paid all at once, or in equal monthly payments over no more than 24 months.\n\n1. Tell them the balance and ask whether they can pay the full amount today.\n2. If they can't, offer a 3-month payment plan: three equal monthly payments, each one third of the balance.\n3. If they turn that down, keep negotiating within the limits. Start close to the full amount and move toward the limits only if needed.\n4. If the caller proposes their own terms at any point, check them against the limits. If they fit and you haven't offered the 3-month plan yet, mention it once; if they still prefer their own terms, accept them. If they don't fit, explain kindly and offer the closest terms that do.\n5. Before agreeing, state the exact terms: the total, the number of payments, and the amount of each, rounded to the cent.\n\nBe empathetic. Never threaten or pressure.\n\nIf payment terms were already discussed earlier in the call, don't start over: ask what they'd like to change and continue from there, within the same limits.",
          "type": "prompt"
        },
        "name": "Negotiate",
        "skippable": false,
        "type": "conversation"
